---
.title = "Read large files with direct file I/O",
.date = "2024-01-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

The low-level `File.readStreaming` and `File.writeStreamingAll` APIs operate directly on files.
The loop processes one fixed-size chunk at a time, so the complete file never has to be held in
memory. “Direct” here means using the file API rather than a higher-level buffered abstraction;
it does not request the operating system's `O_DIRECT` mode, so normal filesystem caching still
applies.

